== the company is short of hands for the spring show
tier: everyday
sphere: arts
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 20-85
calls: RW
rate: 1
tone: mixed
life: leisure, community
horizon: months
roles: colleague, regular, friend
cast_want: asked_help
earth: the amateur company you have followed for years is short of hands for its spring show, and the director asks whether you could give it a few weekends
gap: 3-8
scene: The amateur company at {place} puts on one big show each spring, and this year it is short of hands: someone to build the set, run the lights, sell tickets at the door. {N} has been a face in the audience and at the drinks after the show for years. The director catches {N} at the bar and asks whether {N} could give the company a few weekends.
scene W: A show lives or dies on the people nobody sees, and the company has been short for two seasons now.
scene U: {N} has always wondered how the lights and the set are done, and here is a way to find out.
scene B: Being in with the company means being in with the people who decide who gets seen.
scene R: The thought of being backstage on a first night makes {Ns} heart beat faster.
scene G: These are {Ns} people, the same faces every spring, and the show is the town's own.
- W | take the ticket desk for every night of the run | v: conformity, benevolence | lever: loyalty | foot: place arts.stage | chance: 85
- U | learn the lighting desk from the company's old technician | v: achievement, self-direction | lever: loyalty | foot: person mentor | chance: 75
- B | offer to handle the publicity, with a credit in the programme | v: achievement, power | lever: voice | foot: person patron | chance: 75
- R | say yes, and talk the director into a small part on stage as well | v: stimulation, self-direction | lever: voice | foot: person friend | chance: 65
- G | build the set with the old crew, over the long weekends before the show | v: tradition, benevolence | lever: loyalty | foot: place arts.craft | chance: 85
- W>G | draw up a proper rota, so the old hands finally get a rest | v: benevolence, conformity | lever: loyalty | foot: means time-.06 | chance: 80
- U>W | keep the weekends, but offer to train two new volunteers one evening | v: universalism, achievement | lever: voice | foot: means time+.03 | chance: 80
- B>U | agree, if the company will try reading a new play next season | v: power, self-direction | lever: voice | foot: person colleague | chance: 70
- R>B | decline cheerfully, keeping the weekends for painting of one's own | v: self-direction, hedonism | lever: exit | foot: door turned down a chance | chance: 90
- G>R | bring the family along and make the set-building a weekend party | v: hedonism, tradition | lever: loyalty | foot: means ties+.06 | chance: 80
works: The spring show goes up on time, and at the party afterwards the director raises a glass in {Ns} direction.
works: The company gets through the season with the hands it needs, and {N} is glad of the answer given.
fails: The run is chaotic, a cue goes missing on the first night, and everyone backstage is short-tempered for a week.
fails: The arrangement {N} offered does not quite fit, and the director is asking around again by the next spring.

