earth: the director of the choir you have sung in for years is stepping down, and the committee asks you to take the baton
gap: 3-8
scene: For years {N} has sung at {place}, in the middle row, rarely missing a week. Now the director is stepping down after twenty seasons, and the committee asks {N} to take the baton: the weekly practice, the choice of music, the winter concert that half the town comes to.
scene W: A choir needs someone who starts on time, knows every part and treats every voice alike.
scene U: {N} would want to learn the craft properly first: reading scores, shaping a sound, keeping time for forty.
scene B: The director of the town's choir is somebody, and {N} would be the one people thank on concert night.
scene R: {N} has always wanted the choir to sing something that makes people cry, not only nod along.
scene G: The choir has its old pieces, sung every winter for longer than anyone can remember.
- W | take the baton, and keep practice to the same hour and the same rules each week | v: conformity, security | lever: lead | lead: rules | foot: place arts.song | chance: 75
- U | take a conducting course first, then take the choir in the new year | v: achievement, self-direction | lever: lead | lead: knowing | foot: place learn.higher | chance: 70
- B | agree, and ask for the director's name on the concert posters | v: power, achievement | lever: lead | lead: favours | foot: person rival | chance: 65
- R | say yes, and open the winter concert with something new and wild | v: stimulation, self-direction | lever: lead | lead: inspiring | foot: place gather.great | chance: 65
- G | stay in the middle row, and put forward the oldest alto instead | v: tradition, benevolence | lever: loyalty | foot: person elder | chance: 85
- W>U | share the post with the accompanist, each with set duties | v: conformity, universalism | lever: lead | foot: person colleague | chance: 75
- U>B | lead the choir, and enter it in the regional competition | v: achievement, power | lever: lead | lead: knowing | foot: means time-.10 | chance: 60
- B>R | decline the post, but offer to sing the solos at every concert | v: hedonism, power | lever: voice | foot: means time+.03 | chance: 80
- R>G | say no kindly, since leading would spoil the joy of simply singing | v: hedonism, tradition | lever: neglect | foot: door turned down a chance | chance: 90
- G>W | agree for one season, to keep the winter concert going while they look | v: tradition, conformity | lever: loyalty | foot: door kept your word | chance: 80
works: The winter concert fills the hall again, and the old director, in the front row, is seen wiping an eye.
works: The choir settles into its new shape within a season, and the middle row is as full as ever.
fails: Two of the strongest voices leave over the changes, and the winter concert is thinner than anyone hoped.
fails: The first practices are awkward, and for a few months the choir sounds like a room of strangers.

