- G | put forward the founder of the house, now old, and sit beside them | v: tradition, benevolence | lever: loyalty | foot: person elder | chance: 80
- W>B | agree, if the artists will first choose their speaker by a fair vote | v: universalism, power | lever: voice | foot: place gather.hall | chance: 75
- U>R | decline the microphone, but write the open letter the others will read | v: self-direction, universalism | lever: voice | foot: place arts.page | chance: 80
- B>G | agree, and invite the councillors to an opening night first | v: power, tradition | lever: lead | lead: favours | foot: person patron | chance: 65
- R>W | decline, saying the work should speak for itself | v: self-direction, universalism | lever: exit | foot: door turned down a chance | chance: 90
- G>U | ask the oldest members what saved the house last time, and say that | v: tradition, achievement | lever: loyalty | foot: person mentor | chance: 70
works: The cut is halved at the meeting, and the local paper runs a picture of {place} with its doors open.
works: The artists come away feeling their case was made well, and they say so to {N} in their different ways.
fails: The council listens, thanks everyone for coming, and passes the cut as it stood.
fails: The meeting turns sour, and the artists spend the next month arguing among themselves about what went wrong.

