scene W: The fair pays for the club's whole year, and it only happens because someone turns up.
scene U: {N} has noticed that the fair loses money on the same things every year.
scene B: Whoever runs a stall gets to know everybody on the street, and everybody gets to know them.
scene R: A street full of music and people on a summer day is {Ns} idea of a good time.
scene G: The fair is older than most of the houses on the street, and the old families still run the cake stall.
