- U>G | lend the club tools and tables, but keep the Saturdays free | v: benevolence, security | lever: fund | foot: means time+.03 | chance: 90
- B>W | agree, in exchange for a place on the club's committee | v: power, conformity | lever: voice | foot: place rule.counsel | chance: 70
- R>U | say no this year, with a promise to think about next summer | v: hedonism, self-direction | lever: exit | foot: door turned down a chance | chance: 90
- G>B | bring the whole family to run a stall together | v: tradition, achievement | lever: loyalty | foot: means ties+.06 | chance: 80
works: The fair is the best in years, and on the evening of it the whole street is still out in the warm air.
works: The club gets the help it needs, and the secretary thanks {N} at the next meeting in front of everyone.
fails: Rain comes in at noon, the stalls are packed away early, and the takings barely cover the band.
fails: The arrangement {N} offered does not quite fit, and the secretary is still a pair of hands short on the day.

