horizon: years
roles: neighbour, colleague, rival
earth: the tenants' movement {N} leads must choose its one demand
scene: Rents in town have risen every year for five, and the tenants' movement that meets at {place} has grown from a dozen to a thousand. Now it must choose one demand to fight for, and the meeting waits on {N}.
- R | march for a freeze on every rent in town, starting now | v: stimulation, benevolence | scope: town_sphere | lever: voice | chance: 50
- W>U | press for a rent board across the country, with open, published rules | v: universalism, security | scope: nation | lever: lead | chance: 40
- G>B | settle street by street with the landlords who know their tenants | v: security, tradition | scope: place | lever: loyalty | chance: 70
- U | pass the council's own empty-homes figures to the movement, quietly, before they are published | v: self-direction, universalism | scope: town_sphere | lever: subvert | chance: 60
works: The demand is heard, and within a year some rents in town have stopped climbing.
works: The movement holds together through the fight, and more people come to {place} than ever.
fails: The landlords hold firm, and the movement loses half its members over the winter.
fails: The demand splits the meeting, and two groups now claim to speak for the tenants.

